### 4.2 Who does what
| Platform (built once) | Game (built per game) |
|---|---|
| Hub, game cards, search, filters, favorites | Game rules, physics, maps, scoring |
| Room codes, join links, QR, passwords, **open rooms list, quick join**, kick, ban, host migration and transfer, reconnect (60 s), spectators, late-join queue | Game state, bots, results data |
| Lobby shell: players, teams (game says team sizes), ready, chat, invite, settings form built from `settingsSchema` | Mode cards, map cards, map preview art, extras for the lobby |
| InputManager and Control Setup screen built from the game's control styles | Which logical actions mean what in this game |
| Match state machine `LOBBY -> LOADING -> COUNTDOWN -> PLAYING -> RESULTS` | In-game scene (Phaser), HUD, effects, sounds |
| Results screen, scoreboard component, toasts, modals, settings, profile, command palette | Result columns, awards |
| Socket handling, validation, rate limits, snapshot transport | Input validation and the simulation step |
| PWA, offline cache, fullscreen, wake lock, audio unlock | Asset list (lazy loaded) |

### 4.3 Lazy loading
Each game loads with a dynamic `import()` only when the player opens it. The Hub must load in under 2 seconds on 4G (under 300 KB of JS before games).

### 4.4 Platform API version
`PLATFORM_API = 1` in `/platform/shared/config.ts`. Each game declares `requires: 1`. If the platform changes in a breaking way the number goes up and old games show "needs update". This keeps 30 games safe.

