## 5. HOW TO ADD A GAME (30-game readiness)

### 5.1 The GameModule interface (`/platform/shared/GameModule.ts`)
```ts
interface GameModule {
  id: string;                          // "tank-arena" (lowercase, dashes, unique)
  requires: number;                    // platform API version
  meta: {
    name: string; tagline: string; description: string;
    icon: string;                      // 512x512 PNG path
    banner: string;                    // 1280x720 PNG path
    tags: string[];                    // "action", "party", "strategy", "quick", "team"...
    minPlayers: number; maxPlayers: number; defaultMaxPlayers: number;
    maxSpectators: number;
    maxLocalPlayers: number;           // players on one screen in Local Party (Tank Arena: 4)
    teamSize?: { min: number; max: number };   // per team, for team modes (Tank Arena: 1 to 6)
    avgMinutes: number;                // shown on the card
    supports: { online: boolean; localParty: boolean; solo: boolean };
    devices: { keyboardMouse: boolean; touch: boolean; gamepad: boolean };
  };
  modes: ModeDef[];                    // id, name, plan text, tip, illustration, team type, min/max players
  maps?: MapDef[];                     // id, name, thumbnail, bestFor, recommendedPlayers, description
  settingsSchema: SettingDef[];        // the lobby settings form is BUILT from this
  presets?: PresetDef[];
  controlStyles: ControlStyleDef[];    // id, name, devices, bindings, demo animation, recommended flag
  controls: ControlsDoc;               // per device list of {input, action, hint}
  howTo: HowToDoc;                     // steps with images
  results: ResultsSchema;              // columns for the results screen, award rules
  assets: AssetDef[];                  // lazy-loaded files, with code-drawn fallbacks
  tickRate: number;                    // sim Hz (30 for real time, 0 for turn based)
  createServerRoom(ctx: RoomContext): GameRoom;
  createClientScene(ctx: ClientContext): GameClient;
  createBot?(difficulty: string): BotBrain;
}
interface GameRoom {
  onPlayerJoin(p): void; onPlayerLeave(p): void; onReconnect(p): void;
  onLateJoin?(p): boolean;                               // may refuse (returns false)
  onInput(playerId: string, payload: unknown): void;     // payload belongs to the game
  tick(dt: number): void;
  getSnapshot(): unknown;
  getEvents(): unknown[];
  isFinished(): MatchResult | null;
}
```

### 5.2 Logical actions (so every game works on every device)
| Logical action | Keyboard / mouse | Touch | Gamepad |
|---|---|---|---|
| `move` (x, y, -1 to 1) | W A S D / arrows | virtual stick (left side) | left stick |
| `look` (x, y or angle) | mouse position | virtual stick (right side) or touch point | right stick |
| `primary` (press, hold, release) | left mouse click or Space (per style) | big on-screen button or tap anywhere | A button / RT |
| `secondary` | right mouse click or Shift | second on-screen button | B button |
| `action1` to `action4` | Q E R F or Space (per style) | extra on-screen buttons | X Y LB RB |
| `pause` | Esc | menu button | Start |
Each **ControlStyleDef** says how raw input maps to these actions for one device. The platform draws only the on-screen controls the chosen style needs and builds the Control Setup screen (8.13) from the styles.

### 5.3 Add-a-game checklist (every new game, in order)
1. Copy `/games/_template` to `/games/<new-id>`.
2. Fill `meta`, `modes`, `settingsSchema`, `controlStyles`, `controls`, `howTo`, `results`, `assets`.
3. Write the shared simulation (pure functions, no browser or Node dependencies) with unit tests.
4. Write `createServerRoom` and `createClientScene`.
5. Add one line in `/games/registry.ts`.
6. Check: Hub card, Game Detail page, Create Room, Open rooms, lobby form built from the schema, Control Setup, Local Party and Solo if declared.
7. Run the game QA template (Section 23).
8. Update `docs/GAMES.md` and `credits.json`.
**Acceptance rule:** if you had to edit any file inside `/platform` to add the game (other than the registry line), the platform is not ready; fix the platform first.

### 5.4 Registry example
```ts
// /games/registry.ts
export const GAMES = [
  () => import('./tank-arena/module'),
  // () => import('./next-game/module'),   // add one line per game
];
```

### 5.5 The Hub with 30 games
Responsive grid of game cards; filters (All, Action, Party, Strategy, Quick under 5 min, Team, 2 players, 3 to 4 players, 5 or more players, Favorites); search; sort (Recently played, A to Z, New). "New" ribbon for 14 days; "Coming soon" cards (data only). Assets and code load only when a game is opened.

