| **Rooms** | 4-letter code (no I, O, L), invite link `?room=ABCD`, QR code, **room name**, **private or open**, optional password, **max players (set by the host, within the game's range)**, host, kick, ban, host migration and transfer |
| **Friends joining** | The host shares the code or link (Copy, Share, WhatsApp, QR, Slack/Teams text). Friends open the link or type the code. Everyone appears live in the lobby |
| **Open rooms** | A list of open (not private) rooms on this server with room name, game, host, players x/y, status and a lock icon. Updates every 5 s. Private rooms never appear |
| **Quick Join** | Joins the open room of that game with free seats and the most players waiting; if none, offers Create Room |
| Lobby | Player list with ready checks and control-style icons, team columns, chat with quick messages, game settings (host edits, others read-only), map preview, invite panel, spectator list |
| Chat | Text up to 80 characters, 1 per second, 6 quick messages ("Ready!", "Wait for me", "GG", "Nice shot!", "Again?", "Brb"), light filter that replaces a short word list with `***` |
| Spectators | Up to 20. Join a running match as a viewer; "Take a seat" button appears when a seat is free |
| Late join | Allowed while the game says it is safe (Tank Arena: first 70% of the match time, not in sudden death); the player enters at the next respawn |
| Reconnect | A dropped player can rejoin the same seat for 60 s |
| Rematch | Keeps players and settings; the host may change settings first |
| Settings | Audio, graphics, controls, accessibility, data (Section 20) |
| PWA | Install button, offline Local Party and Solo, update prompt |
| Command palette | `Ctrl/Cmd + K` on desktop (7.9) |
| Credits | Lists every third-party asset |

### 6.2 Room options (platform form, shown when creating a room and editable in the lobby by the host)
| Option | Range | Default |
|---|---|---|
| Room name | 1 to 24 characters | "<nickname>'s room" |
| Visibility | Private (code or link only) / Open (listed) | Private |
| Password | none or 4 to 12 characters | none |
| Max players | the game's min to max (Tank Arena 2 to 12) | the game's default (Tank Arena 8) |
| Spectators | On / Off (up to 20) | On |
| Late join | On / Off | On |
| Start rule | Host starts / Auto-start when everyone is ready (5 s, cancelable) | Host starts |
The host cannot set Max players below the number of players already in the room.

### 6.3 Ready and start rules
- START needs at least the game's minimum players (and, in team modes, at least 1 player or bot on each team).
- The button shows "Start (5/6 ready)". If not everyone is ready the host sees "Start anyway?": players who are not ready **watch this match** as spectators and return to their seat in the lobby afterwards.
- Changing any setting clears everyone's Ready. A player who changes team, style or color also clears their own Ready.

### 6.4 Roles in a room
Host (crown), Player, Spectator, Bot. The host can: edit settings, kick, ban (blocks the player for the life of the room), **transfer host** to another human, close the room. If the host leaves, the earliest-joined human becomes host (toast).

