## 12. GAME 1: TANK ARENA (rules)

### 12.1 Summary
2D top-down tank battles on one screen. Matches last 2 to 4 minutes. Modes: **Flag**, **Team Fight**, **Free For All**. **2 to 12 tanks online** (humans and bots), teams up to **6v6**; Local Party up to 4. Spectators up to 20. The simulation is a fixed step 1/30 s in `/games/tank-arena/shared/sim.ts`; the same code runs in the server, in the browser prediction, in Local Party and in Solo.

### 12.2 Controls and movement
- Movement follows Section 10.8 for the player's control style. All numbers live in `config.ts`.
- **One-button inputs** (Local Party corner button, one-key mode, touch One-Thumb): the platform decides tap vs hold on the client. Holding longer than the **hold delay (0.1 s)** starts driving; releasing within the **tap time (0.2 s, setting 0.12 to 0.30)** counts as a tap (fire counter +1). A quick tap moves the tank at most 20 px.
- **Separate fire inputs** (Space hold + click, WASD, Mouse Steer, Twin-Thumb, Tank Pad, gamepad): no tap detection and no hold delay; the tank reacts at once.
- **Recoil turn** (ARCADE only, host option, default ON): 30 degrees over 0.12 s per shot, alternating right then left; the counter resets at respawn. A recoil turn is cut short if it would push the hull into a wall.
- **Ammo and cooldown:** a shot needs ammo of 1 or more and the 0.2 s cooldown to be over; otherwise a dry click and **no recoil turn**.
- **Hold to rapid fire:** when on, holding fire repeats shots at the cooldown until ammo is 0.
- The server fires exactly once per increase of `fire`, validates ammo, cooldown, speed and turn rate, and ignores impossible input.

