### 12.6 Modes
**1. FLAG (default)**
- Each team has **one flag** standing beside its **pad**. The pad shows a faint icon of the **enemy flag** (where you deliver it). Teams of 1 to 6 players.
- Touch the **enemy flag** with your tank to carry it (the flag shows on the tank and a cyan ring pulses). Only one tank carries a flag at a time; if two touch it in the same tick, the closer tank wins. Carrier speed 90% (host 70 to 100%). The carrier can still shoot.
- **Capture:** drive onto **your own pad** while carrying. Captures needed to win: **Auto** (1 for up to 4 players, 2 for 5 to 8, 3 for 9 to 12; host 1 to 5).
- Carrier destroyed: the flag **drops** there (pushed out of walls). It returns to its spot after 10 s, or instantly when a tank of its own team touches it.
- "Own flag must be home to capture" = OFF by default (casual); the host can turn it ON. On maps where the flag stands on the pad (Map J) it is always ON.
- At time up: more captures wins; a tie plays 30 s sudden death (first capture wins), then a draw.
- Start: tanks begin in their team's spawn pool near their flag. After a kill, they respawn in the pool.
**2. TEAM FIGHT** (no flags)
- Each destroyed enemy tank = 1 point. Points to win: **Auto** (3 for up to 4 players, 5 for 5 to 8, 8 for 9 to 12; host 3 to 30) or the higher score at time up. Tie: sudden death (next point wins). Teams from 1v1 up to **6v6**.
**3. FREE FOR ALL** (up to 12)
- Every tank alone with its own color and shape badge. 1 point per destroyed enemy; points to win **Auto** as above, or the most points at time up. Best with 3 to 8 players; up to 12 allowed.
**Solo play:** any mode with 1 to 11 bots. Online rooms can also be filled with bots (13.3).

### 12.7 Auto scaling (players = humans + bots)
| Players | Time limit | Points to win | Captures to win |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2 to 4 | 2:00 | 3 | 1 |
| 5 to 8 | 3:00 | 5 | 2 |
| 9 to 12 | 4:00 | 8 | 3 |
"Auto" recalculates in the lobby when players join or leave. A value the host sets by hand is kept and marked "Manual".

### 12.8 Match flow, scoring and results
Plan screen (5 s) -> countdown 3-2-1 and a big "START!" banner -> play -> win condition or time up -> freeze 1.5 s with a WINNER banner and confetti -> Results. Score boxes and timer update live. At 30 s left the timer pulses red; at time up a "TIME!" banner shows.
Per player: points, shots fired, hits, accuracy, flags picked up, captures, returns, deaths, powers collected. Awards: Sharpshooter (best accuracy, at least 5 shots), Flag Hero (most captures), Defender (most flag returns), Survivor (fewest deaths), Collector (most powers). **MVP** = points + 3 x captures + returns. Scoreboard order: points (high first), then deaths (low first), then accuracy.

### 12.9 Spawn pools (many players)
Each map defines **spawn areas** (14.1 to 14.6). At map load the shared code builds, deterministically from the match seed, a **spawn pool** for each team and for Free For All:
1. Candidate points on a 32 px grid inside the spawn area, at least **40 px from any wall, brick or barrier** and **70 px from a flag or pad**.
2. Pick points by **farthest-point sampling**, starting from the map's original start spawns, with a minimum spacing of **64 px** (FFA: 160 px). Create **6 points per team** (12 for Free For All). If a map cannot give enough points, relax spacing to 48 px; if still short, use the free point that is farthest from others.
3. Blue's pool is the **mirror** of Red's (horizontal mirror, or point mirror on map J).
**Choosing a spawn:** among the team's pool, take the free point (no tank within 100 px) that is farthest from the nearest enemy; ties go to the lower index. If every point is blocked, wait up to 1 s, then use the next best. Never the same point twice in a row.

### 12.10 Crowd rules (UI and fairness)
- **Name tags** above every tank (nickname, small font, team-colored outline). Your own tank has a thin ring; at spawn a "YOU" arrow shows for 3 s.
- **Kill feed** under the score bar (online): up to 4 lines, each for 3 s: "Dax > Ria" with weapon icon; older lines fade.
- **Scoreboard** (Tab or a button on touch, and at Results): scrolls for 12 players.
- With more than 8 players the name tags of far enemies fade to 40% opacity (Low quality: hidden beyond 500 px).
- Each map shows its **recommended players** (14.1). More players are allowed ("Crowded but fun").
- **AFK:** a player with no input for 20 s in a match gets an "AFK" tag; after 45 s they become a spectator (the host can turn this off); they keep their seat in the lobby.

