## 15. TANK ARENA BOTS
Bots send the same input as players (`TankInput`, using the STEER style internally: heading + throttle + fire counter) with the same speed and turn caps. They get no extra information, never use aim assist and cannot see through walls.
| Difficulty | Reaction | Aim error | Behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| Easy | 0.6 s | 20 degrees | wanders toward enemies, wastes shells, ignores power boxes |
| Medium | 0.35 s | 10 degrees | targets the nearest enemy, grabs power boxes, avoids shells poorly |
| Hard | 0.15 s | 4 degrees | uses cover, leads shots, hunts the flag carrier, dodges shells |
Method: path on a coarse grid; fire when an enemy is within the aim error in front with a line of sight and ammo is available. **Flag roles:** Attacker (go for the enemy flag), Carrier (shortest safe path to its own pad), Defender (stay within 350 px of its flag), Recoverer (hunt the enemy carrier or touch a dropped own flag); with larger teams the roles are split roughly 40% Attacker, 30% Defender, 30% Recoverer, and only one bot goes for the flag at a time. **Team Fight and FFA:** hunt the weakest visible enemy; retreat toward the spawn area when out of ammo. Bots keep a short random delay so they feel human and are never perfect. Up to 11 bots run in Solo; the server budget for bot thinking is 2 ms per tick per room (bots think in turns when the room has many). Solo and Local Party use the same bot code locally.

