## 21. RULES AND EDGE CASES (implement every row)

**Platform and rooms**
| # | Situation | Required behavior |
|---|---|---|
| P1 | Room full | "Room is full (12/12)" with "Watch as spectator" if allowed |
| P2 | Match in progress | "Match running: watch as spectator", then "Join match" if late join allows |
| P3 | Host leaves | Earliest-joined human becomes host, toast "[name] is now the host" |
| P4 | Player disconnects | Seat held 60 s, game object parked and safe, then removed (score kept as "left") |
| P5 | Duplicate or invalid nickname | Add (2), (3); empty or HTML names become "Player" + 3 digits |
| P6 | Kicked | "You were removed by the host"; cannot rejoin for 60 s |
| P7 | Wrong code or room gone | "Room not found" / "That room no longer exists" |
| P8 | Setting out of range (modified client) | Server clamps to range |
| P9 | One room crashes | try/catch; other rooms continue; error logged |
| P10 | Browser tab hidden | Local Party and Solo pause; online sends neutral input; AFK after 20 s, spectator after 45 s |
| P11 | Window resize, rotation, fullscreen | Rescale instantly, keep state, clear inputs |
| P12 | Offline | Local and Solo work; online buttons disabled with a message |
| P13 | Old cached version | "New version, tap to update" |
| P14 | Audio blocked | "Tap to start"; silent until the first tap |
| P15 | Fullscreen, orientation lock or wake lock unsupported | Hide or show a tip; never an error |
| P16 | Browser back button | Previous screen; during a match a confirm dialog |
| P17 | Clocks differ | Server time offset used for match, respawn and power timers |
| P18 | Lag spike | Extrapolate up to 200 ms, then freeze with a lag icon, blend within 150 ms |
| P19 | Rematch | Scores reset; players, teams, settings kept; leavers removed |
| P20 | Two players want the same key | Conflict warning, second choice rejected |
| P21 | Host lowers Max players below the current count | Not allowed; the control stops at the current count with a tooltip |
| P22 | Two friends take the last seat in the same instant | The server processes in order; the second gets "Room is full" and can watch |
| P23 | An open room fills or starts while listed | The list updates within 5 s; a join attempt is handled by P1 or P2 |
| P24 | Host uses "Make host" | Toast for everyone; the old host stays as a player with no host rights |
| P25 | "Start anyway" with players not ready | They watch this match as spectators and return to their seats in the lobby |
| P26 | Room code collision or unwanted word | A new code is generated; blocklist checked |
| P27 | Spam: many creates, joins or messages | Friendly rate-limit message with a wait time; repeated abuse closes the socket |
| P28 | Many players leave and only 1 human remains in a match | Match continues against bots if any (T15); otherwise ends with "Waiting for players" and returns to the lobby |
| P29 | Open room with a password | Listed with a lock icon; password asked before joining |
| P30 | Everyone in the lobby is a spectator or the host closes the room | The room closes and everyone sees "The host closed the room" |

**Tank Arena**
| # | Situation | Required behavior |
|---|---|---|
| T1 | Two tanks destroy each other on the same tick | Both die; both teams score; if that decides the match it is a draw point and sudden death starts |
| T2 | Shell hits a shielded or spawn-shielded tank | Shell destroyed, shield used (spawn shield only ripples), no kill |
| T3 | Tank spawns where another tank stands | Spawn waits up to 1 s, then uses the next free pool point; never overlaps |
| T4 | Carrier destroyed, disconnects or leaves | Flag drops there (pushed out of walls); returns after the return time or at once when its own team touches it |
| T5 | Carrier reaches own pad but own flag is away (strict ON) | No capture; message "Your flag is taken!"; carrier keeps the flag |
| T6 | Both flags carried at once | Allowed; with strict OFF the first carrier to touch their pad wins |
| T7 | Dead tank touches a power box or flag | No pickup |
| T8 | Two tanks touch a power box or flag on the same tick | Closer tank wins; equal: earlier input time |
| T9 | Power expires while carrying a flag | Normal; carrier slowdown stays |
| T10 | Ammo 0 and player fires | Dry click, no shell, recoil turn does NOT happen |
| T11 | Fire while the tank is pushed into a wall | Recoil turn is cut short at wall contact; the hull never overlaps a wall |
| T12 | Brick destroyed under a tank | A brick cannot be destroyed while a tank touches it |
| T13 | Time up in Flag with equal captures | 30 s sudden death, then a draw |
| T14 | Reaching the win limit | Match ends that tick; later events ignored |
| T15 | Team has 0 humans mid-match | Bots continue if present; otherwise the other team wins by forfeit |
| T16 | Player joins mid-match | Spectator first, then "Join match" if late join is allowed (T24) |
| T17 | Local Party: finger leaves the corner button | Press stays active until the finger lifts (pointer capture) |
| T18 | Local Party: 4 fingers trigger system gestures | Release inputs, show the tip, keep the match paused |
| T19 | Floating point drift | Fixed step, rounded positions, shared seeded random, no `Date.now()` in the step |
| T20 | Missing PNG or sound | Code-drawn fallback, never a blank screen |
| T21 | Spawn pool smaller than the players | Relax spacing to 48 px; then wait 1 s and use the farthest free point; never overlap |
| T22 | A 7th player tries to join a team of 6 | Join button disabled "Team full (6/6)"; the player goes to the other team or spectates |
| T23 | Players join or leave in the lobby with "Auto" settings | Time, points and captures recalculate; manual values stay |
| T24 | Late join during sudden death or after 70% of the time | Not allowed; the player stays a spectator and sees why |
| T25 | Name tags overlap with many tanks | Tags are offset up to 12 px and fade by distance (12.10) |
| T26 | Kill feed overflow (many kills in 1 s) | Show the newest 4; drop older lines |
| T27 | Scoreboard ties | Order by points, then fewer deaths, then accuracy |
| T28 | AFK player holding the flag | The flag drops when they become a spectator (T4) |
| T29 | Bots and humans balance changes (a human joins a team with bots) | The newest bot on the fuller team leaves at its next respawn |
| T30 | Team sizes uneven (for example 6 vs 4) | Allowed with a warning; "Fill with bots: Even teams" fixes it at start |

**Controls**
| # | Situation | Required behavior |
|---|---|---|
| C1 | Keyboard ghosting (several keys at once) | Key test screen; arrow keys as fallback; never a crash |
| C2 | Click on a HUD or menu element during a match | Does not fire |
| C3 | Window loses focus while Space or a stick is held | All inputs release, the tank stops |
| C4 | Space presses a focused button | Focus is blurred at match start and `preventDefault` is used during the match |
| C5 | Finger moves from the stick area to FIRE (or the reverse) | The finger keeps its first role (pointer capture) |
| C6 | More than 2 touches online | Extra touches ignored (Local Party allows 4) |
| C7 | Orientation change mid-match | Controls re-layout; Local Party pauses; online sends neutral input |
| C8 | Change of control style in a match | Only from the pause menu; online it applies from the next respawn; the server validates |
| C9 | Left-handed swap | Mirrors the layout and saves it |
| C10 | Gamepad stick drift | Dead zone 0.2 plus a calibration slider |
| C11 | Mixed control styles in one match | Allowed unless the host locks to Standard; the style icon shows in the lobby |
| C12 | Non-QWERTY keyboard | Physical key codes used; labels follow the layout when available |
| C13 | Edge swipe or Safari back gesture | Controls stay 24 px from edges; one-time tip; browser back asks for confirmation in a match |
| C14 | Input delay above 50 ms | Debug overlay shows input latency; the game never waits for `click` |
| C15 | Mouse leaves the window | Release the fire input; the aim ring stays at the last point |
| C16 | Hold to rapid fire runs ammo to 0 | Dry click, rapid fire stops until a shell returns |

