## 24. DEPLOYMENT AND THE APP

**Google Cloud project error:** if AI Studio shows "Failed to create project... must be created from the Google Cloud console", create a project at console.cloud.google.com with the same Google account and import it in AI Studio. Billing is needed only for deploying the multiplayer server.
**Option 1: AI Studio deploy (Cloud Run):** WebSockets allowed, request timeout 3600 s, **maximum instances = 1** (rooms live in memory, so everyone must reach the same instance), **minimum instances = 1**, at least 1 vCPU and 512 MB, concurrency 80 or higher (each WebSocket holds a connection), a region near you (India: `asia-south1` Mumbai). The server listens on `process.env.PORT` and serves the site and `/ws`.
**Option 2: An office PC as the server (best ping, no internet needed):** install Node.js, run `npm install`, `npm run build`, `npm start`; everyone opens `http://<that PC's IP>:3000` and the port is allowed in the firewall. All friends must be on the same network. (PWA install and wake lock need HTTPS, so use Option 1 or a local HTTPS proxy for those.)
**Option 3:** Render, Railway or Fly.io (check WebSocket support; free tiers may sleep and drop rooms).
**For friends outside the office:** Option 1 or 3 with the public link; share the code or link by WhatsApp.
**PWA:** `manifest.webmanifest` (name Office Arena, icons 192 and 512, `display: fullscreen` with `standalone` fallback), a service worker that caches the shell, the Hub and each game's assets after first use; show "Offline: only Local and Solo" when not connected. Use fullscreen (button), `screen.orientation.lock('landscape')` after fullscreen (ignore failure) and `navigator.wakeLock` during a match (ignore if unsupported). Fullscreen may be unavailable on iPhone Safari: show the tip "Add to Home Screen for full screen" (check this in testing).
**Optional later: store app.** The PWA can be wrapped for the Play Store with a Trusted Web Activity or Capacitor. Not needed for v1.
**Post-deploy smoke test:** two real devices (one PC, one phone): open the Hub, create a room, join by code, link and QR, play Flag on Map A and Team Fight on Map G, try each control style, check ping, reconnect (toggle Wi-Fi), results and rematch, install the PWA, test offline Solo. **Then a friends test:** 6 to 12 people join one room, play a full Flag match and a Free For All on map H; note lag, joins, and any confusion in the lobby.

